From: Indr1d-C0ld <102763446+Indr1d-C0ld@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:26:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] SAGA2: Return nothing when iterating an empty sector
 region

RegionalObjectIterator clamps its sector range to the world, so a search
outside the map gives an empty range. first() still read the sector at
the minimum coordinates, which getSector() maps to an unrelated sector,
and could return its objects; the following next() then failed its
range assertion.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 engines/saga2/objects.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engines/saga2/objects.cpp b/engines/saga2/objects.cpp
index f255de20..2f9bc8b2 100644
--- a/engines/saga2/objects.cpp
+++ b/engines/saga2/objects.cpp
@@ -3391,6 +3391,13 @@ ObjectID SectorRegionObjectIterator::first(GameObject **obj) {
 
 	_currentObject = nullptr;
 
+	//  A region outside the world is clamped to an empty range: searching it
+	//  would read an unrelated sector and leave the iterator out of range.
+	if (_minSector.u >= _maxSector.u || _minSector.v >= _maxSector.v) {
+		if (obj != nullptr) *obj = nullptr;
+		return Nothing;
+	}
+
 	_sectorCoords = _minSector;
 	currentSector = _searchWorld->getSector(_sectorCoords.u, _sectorCoords.v);
 
